  "summary": "I'm a soon-to-be Cornell University graduate (May 2025) with a passion for creating innovative software solutions. My journey so far includes valuable internships at Capital One, where I honed my skills in building robust, data-driven applications, and rewarding experiences as a Teaching Assistant for Computer Science classes ranging from Data Structures to Natural Language Processing and AI, where I helped my peers grasp complex programming concepts.\n\nI've also had the exciting opportunity to lead an AI-integrated startup, diving into both frontend and backend development while working with technologies like Python, TypeScript, and PyTorch. These experiences have taught me to thrive in collaborative environments and fueled my eagerness to continue learning and growing as I transition from academia to the professional world.\n\nI'm eager to connect with fellow tech enthusiasts and industry professionals to share ideas, learn new skills, and contribute to projects that make a real impact!",
